<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Staraya Ladoga</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aldeigjuborg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Staraya Ladoga is a village on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volkhov-river">Volkhov</a> river near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, on the site of one of the earliest towns of Rus'. Founded around 753 as a trading settlement where Scandinavians, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finns">Finns</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> met, it lay on the river routes to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>. One version of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> names it as the first seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rurik">Rurik</a>.</p></div>
